##! Please refer to the documentation at
##! https://coreruleset.org/docs/development/regex_assembly/.

##! This list excludes command words that are prone to cause false
##! positives from the following include files:
##!
##! - unix-shell-upto3.ra
##! - unix-shell-4andup.ra
##! - unix-shell-pl3.ra

##! PL1-only companion of unix-shell-fps-useragents.ra: common English
##! words that double as short Unix commands, reported as false positives
##! in request filenames, referers and user-agents (issues #4761, #4895).
##! Verified firing-on-main FP forms: `who we are`, `/who-we-serve/` and
##! the locale tag `(es-es)`.
##! These words stay excluded from PL1 headers/filenames only — the PL2
##! rule 932239 keeps full coverage, so probes such as `;es -c id` and
##! `;who -a` are still caught there.

who
who@
who~
es
es@
es~
